<task id="039" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>External event reads for Matter and Work Assignment (FR-03 server)</title>
    <phase>3 BFF features</phase>
    <gate>after 032 and 037</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New external read routes (tags bff-api, auth)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Direct generalization following the to-do route pattern in the same file</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file chain on ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs (030 → 031 → 032 → 039) and ExternalDataService.cs (after 035, 037)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>032, 037</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add GET /api/v1/external/matters/{id}/events and /workassignments/{id}/events so the detail view can show events for every root type that has them, exactly as /projects/{id}/events does.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ASP.NET Core developer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Event reads exist for projects, matters and workassignments with the same Read check and DTO; tests cover access and denial.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-03 shows events/tasks through the existing external reads. To-dos already exist for projects, matters and workassignments (ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:127-:181), but events only for projects (:215 GET, :223 POST). Without this the detail view cannot show events on a Matter or Work Assignment. Document, Invoice and Service Request detail views show no events section (decision recorded in notes/decisions.md).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectEventContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRootEventReadTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every route this task adds or modifies is mapped inside the /api/v1/external group (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:60-63) so it inherits the ExternalCollaboration policy and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. No route in this task is mapped outside that group.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No OBO on the external plane: every Dataverse and SPE call this task adds is app-only and scoped to the caller's accessible set (spec NFR-01).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build: more than +5 MB needs written justification; the total must stay at or under 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build only on the net10 SDK (10.0.1xx). Run /conflict-check before opening the PR: Api/ExternalAccess/** and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** are shared with unified-access-control-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Generalize the project event read over the RightsForRoot pattern (ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:535) used by to-dos; do not copy the handler per type.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Read only; event create stays project-only in this task.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>external event reads</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
