  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the project event read handler and the to-do RightsForRoot generalization.</step>
    <step order="2">Generalize the event read over projects/matters/workassignments and map the two new routes.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests: accessible matter/WA → events; outside the set → 403; ViewOnly → allowed (read).</step>
    <step order="4">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="6">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-039-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If sprk_event has no lookup to sprk_matter or sprk_workassignment that the project read's filter can use, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>GET /projects/{id}/events at ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:215.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — the existing handler is generalized over the root map; only two route templates are new.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The record detail view shows no events for Matters and Work Assignments (FR-03).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRootEventReadTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/v1/external/matters/{id}/events and /workassignments/{id}/events return that record's events for a caller with Read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both return 403 for a record outside the caller's set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /projects/{id}/events behaviour and its contract tests are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

